From a49c58e0bcbb01a534d314757d8a5dbcead9f65e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 23:45:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] network/TCPServer: refuse a connection that select() cannot
 watch

The server watches its connections with select(), whose fd_set holds the
descriptors below FD_SETSIZE (1024) only, and FD_SET() on a higher one
writes past the set: without _FORTIFY_SOURCE, as Kodi is built here, it
overwrites the server thread's stack, and with it glibc aborts the
process. Kodi's service allows it 16384 descriptors, so once enough files
and sockets are open, a new JSON-RPC connection (or many of them from one
client on the network) gets a descriptor above it.

Such a connection is now closed at once, with a line in the log, and the
server goes on serving the others. A Kodi that has more than a thousand
descriptors open has a problem of its own to look at; the connection
cannot be served safely by select() either way.
---
 xbmc/network/TCPServer.cpp | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/xbmc/network/TCPServer.cpp b/xbmc/network/TCPServer.cpp
index 54abe83..0a40efb 100644
--- a/xbmc/network/TCPServer.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/network/TCPServer.cpp
@@ -347,6 +347,20 @@ void CTCPServer::Process()
               break;
             }
           }
+#if !defined(TARGET_WINDOWS)
+          else if (newconnection->m_socket >= FD_SETSIZE)
+          {
+            // select() watches descriptors below FD_SETSIZE only, and FD_SET on a higher one
+            // writes past the set. Kodi may have that many open (its service allows more), so the
+            // connection is refused rather than watched.
+            CLog::Log(LOGERROR,
+                      "JSONRPC Server: Refused a connection, its descriptor {} is beyond the {} "
+                      "that can be watched",
+                      newconnection->m_socket, FD_SETSIZE);
+            closesocket(newconnection->m_socket);
+            newconnection->m_socket = INVALID_SOCKET;
+          }
+#endif
           else
           {
             CLog::Log(LOGINFO, "JSONRPC Server: New connection added");
-- 
2.53.0

